id: illusion-smash
name: Illusion Smash
uaType: magical
prerequisite: Portal Creation
tpCost: 10
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCostPerTier: 3
# "Target an Opponent, you can make a Basic Attack Maneuver against that Opponent as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver. If you
# do, treat them as if they were on a Square adjacent to you for this Attacking Maneuver" - no Melee Range or reach
# refusing it, no Long Range on it - "and this Attacking Maneuver cannot possess an AoE". Whom asked
# (use-maneuver.mjs askSmash), thrown at once (chat.mjs postSmash). "Ignore the second effect of Giant Strike": Giant
# Strike is not in this system, so there is nothing to ignore yet.
smashes: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A Basic Attack Out-of-Sequence at an Opponent as if they stood beside you - no Long Range, no AoE.
text: >
  Illusion Smash: You can attack from a distance as though you were in close range, utilizing portals or other magical
  means.
  –Ability Type: Magical
  –Prerequisites: Portal Creation
  –TP Cost: 10
  –KP Cost: 3(T)
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –Minions: N/A
  –Passive Bonus: N/A
  –Effect: Target an Opponent, you can make a Basic Attack Maneuver against that Opponent as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver.
  If you do, treat them as if they were on a Square adjacent to you for this Attacking Maneuver. Ignore the second
  effect of Giant Strike for this Attacking Maneuver and this Attacking Maneuver cannot possess an AoE.
